      "gloss": "I don't believe so / I don't think so",
      "note": "common negative response"
    }
  ],
  "concepts": [
    {
      "id": "c-croire-to-believe-to",
      "term": "{croire} = to believe / to think",
      "definition": "Express belief or softer opinions - often used like penser but more tentative",
      "example": "{je crois que c'est vrai} (I believe it's true), {tu crois?} (do you think so?)"
    },
    {
      "id": "c-irregular-conjugation",
      "term": "Irregular conjugation",
      "definition": "Present: je crois, tu crois, il croit, nous croyons, vous croyez, ils croient",
      "example": "Notice: singular all same sound ('kwa'), {nous}/vous have y, ils have -ient"
    },
    {
      "id": "c-croire-que-to-believe",
      "term": "{croire que...} (to believe that...)",
      "definition": "Like penser que, use with '{que}' to introduce what you believe",
      "example": "{je crois que oui} (I believe so), {je ne crois pas} (I don't believe so / I don't think so)"
    },
    {
      "id": "c-croire-a-croire-en",
      "term": "{croire à} / {croire en} (to believe in)",
      "definition": "Use à or en to express belief in concepts or things",
      "example": "{je crois en toi} (I believe in you), {je crois à ça} (I believe in that)"
    },
    {
      "id": "c-penser-vs-croire",
      "term": "penser vs croire",
      "definition": "penser = think (more definite), croire = believe (more tentative/hopeful)",
      "example": "{je pense qu'il vient} (I think he's coming - pretty sure), {je crois qu'il vient} (I believe he's coming - less certain)"
    }
  ],
